  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe gate now writes the reason when a direct test executable stops without an exit code. A signal can kill the process, or the process can stop on a crash status. Before this change, the step log and the step note showed only `exit -1`.\n\n- New module `xtask/src/exit_status.rs`. On Unix it names the signal and the core dump (`killed by signal 11 (SIGSEGV), core dumped`). On Windows it names the known crash statuses (`status 0xC0000005 (access violation)`).\n- `direct::run` writes a line `gate: the test executable stopped: <how>` into the step log.\n- `exec::read_log` puts the reason into the step note: `FAIL 1s ui suites: trace_parity exit -1 (killed by signal 11 (SIGSEGV))`.\n\nThe PR adds no host lock. The decision is in `docs/decisions/3258-gate-names-the-crash.md`.\n\n## Root cause of #3258 (evidence)\n\nThe repository has no shared resource that two runs on one host use at the same time. The cause was a hardware Vulkan driver on the runner hosts. That cause is outside the repository, and the runner environment fixed it.\n\n- Each red UI step stopped in the middle of its tests, with no panic. I compared each log with a green log of the same binary. The tests that did not finish are the GPU tests:\n  - trace_parity (egg, 44950073227): `the_gpu_sees_the_box_the_cpu_sees` and `deviation_classes_agree_with_the_cpu_verdict`.\n  - egui_app (wopr, 44955923206): `a_headless_start_with_a_model_file_imports_and_draws_it`, `egui_headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero` and `a_headless_start_with_a_project_file_opens_and_draws_it`.\n- `exit -1` is the gate's value for \"no exit code\": a signal killed the process (`st.code().unwrap_or(-1)` in `direct::run`).\n- mkinney's kernel logs show a segfault in `libvulkan.so` on skull and egg at the failure times. The runners pinned Mesa's software Vulkan at about 22:40 UTC. All three UI failures came before that time.\n- mkinney found no kernel segfault and no OOM on wopr. The wopr abort is attributed to the driver only by its time (before the 22:40 UTC pin), not by a log line.\n- About 30 post-merge runs came after the pin, and many of them ran at the same time. None of them has a UI `exit -1`. The red runs between 02:41 and 04:10 are deterministic test failures (`slot_dxf_sketch`, `example_catalog`), not this signature.\n- The uma failure (44987903117, `bore_core`) has a different cause. It was `PermissionDenied` on a PID-named directory in a shared `/tmp`, and #3290 fixed it.\n\nThe two runner-level stops with no log are not covered: the skull run that hung (44982953354) and the uma run that lost communication with the server (44995766211, attempt 1). Follow-up #3303 tracks them.\n\n## Tests\n\n- The pin reserves its temp directory with an atomic `create_dir` and steps past `AlreadyExists`, as `fixture_dir` in `crates/app/tests/bore_core.rs` does (#3290).\n- Pin: `exit_status::tests::a_crashed_step_executable_says_how_it_stopped_in_its_log_and_note`. It runs a crashing child through `direct::run`: `sh -c 'kill -SEGV $$'` on Unix, and `cmd /c exit -1073741819` on Windows. I removed the `direct.rs` change, and the pin failed (`no stop line in: Running crash (cmd)`). With the fix, the pin passes.\n- `a_signal_death_names_the_signal_and_the_core_dump` (Unix), `a_crash_status_names_the_crash` (Windows), `a_plain_exit_code_has_no_crash_words`, `the_note_carries_how_the_executable_stopped`.\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: green on Windows.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: green on 8f1f47035 (xtask unit tests, 183 s, 0 failed).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- I ran the tests on Windows only. The Unix test and the Unix branch of the pin will run on the post-merge runner.\n- The historical abort was not reproduced. The new line shows its signal on the next occurrence.\n\nChangelog: none (gate tooling: a step that a signal kills now names the signal in its log and note)\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #3258\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n",
